cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "ModLearn Lab: stepwise mathematics tutoring with a locally hosted language model"
authors:
  - family-names: Schroffenegger
    given-names: Thomas
    affiliation: "Pädagogische Hochschule Vorarlberg"
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-11-01"
license: EUPL-1.2
repository-code: "https://github.com/harubert/modlearn-lab"
abstract: >-
  Web platform of the ModLearn Technology Lab at the Pädagogische Hochschule
  Vorarlberg. Children get graded help with mathematics tasks from a language
  model that runs on the institution's own hardware behind a private network;
  teachers run the sessions, put tasks into them and read every dialogue.
  An optional, teacher-enabled quality-assurance path sends only masked task
  text to an external model. Includes the benchmark of the help pipeline
  with 60 own tasks and simulated children.
keywords:
  - mathematics education
  - intelligent tutoring
  - large language models
  - privacy
  - Django
